13. Predict the Output – ADT Using Structure
#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
struct Stack {
int data[3];
int top;
};
int main() {
struct Stack s = {{10, 20, 30}, 2};
printf(&quot;%d&quot;, s.data[s.top]);
return 0;
}
Question: Predict the output and identify the current top element.

13. ADT Using Structure
Structure:
data = {10, 20, 30}
top = 2
Array indexes:
Index:  0   1   2
Data:  10  20  30
The statement:
s.data[s.top]
becomes:
s.data[2]
Therefore:
30
Output:
30
Current top element: 30
E. Recursion
